<h2 id="creating-a-branch-for-every-preview-environment" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Creating a branch for every Preview environment</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#creating-a-branch-for-every-preview-environment" aria-label="Link to Creating a branch for every Preview environment"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2>
<p>Neon offers an <a href="https://api-docs.neon.tech/reference/getting-started-with-neon-api?utm_source=devday&amp;utm_medium=blogpost&amp;utm_campaign=blog">API</a> that you can use to manage resources programmatically. You can use it along with a CI/CD tool to achieve the following flow:</p>
<ol>
<li>A developer will work on changes locally against a local Postgres instance or a Neon branch. These changes could potentially include schema changes.</li>
<li>They will then open a pull request which triggers a CI/CD workflow that does the following:<!-- -->
<ol>
<li>Creates a Neon branch</li>
<li>Applies database migrations if there are any</li>
<li>Creates a preview deployment and uses the newly created Neon branch for the database</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li>If everything looks good in the preview environment, the developer will merge their changes. This will trigger another CI/CD workflow that deploys the app to production. This workflow does the following:<!-- -->
<ol>
<li>Applies the database migrations to the primary Neon branch</li>
<li>Creates a production deployment</li>
<li>Deletes the old Neon preview branch, which is no longer needed</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ol>
<p><span aria-owns="rmiz-modal-" data-rmiz=""><span data-rmiz-content="not-found" style="visibility:visible"><img src="https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/creating-a-branch-for-every-preview-environment-1024x576-b99cb9f4.png" alt="Image"/></span></span></p>
<h2 id="seeing-the-flow-in-action" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Seeing the flow in action</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#seeing-the-flow-in-action" aria-label="Link to Seeing the flow in action"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2>
<h3 id="setting-up-the-demo-project-locally" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight"><span>Setting up the demo project locally</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#setting-up-the-demo-project-locally" aria-label="Link to Setting up the demo project locally"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h3>
<p>To see the flow in action, we created a demo app that displays the data coming from the <code>elements</code> table that we created previously. The app is built using <a href="https://nextjs.org/">Next.js</a>, <a href="https://prisma.io">Prisma</a>, and Neon and is deployed to Vercel.</p>
<p>For our CI/CD pipeline for this project, we’ll use GitHub Actions, which are automated workflows that you define as code. These workflows are written in YAML, and they live in a <code>.github</code> folder inside your project’s repository.</p>
<p>To clone the demo app locally, run the following command:</p>
<figure class="code-block group/code-block relative flex flex-col [&amp;_pre]:min-w-full" data-has-filename="false"><pre class="shiki css-variables" style="background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)" tabindex="0" data-language="bash"><code class="grid"><span class="line" data-line="1"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-function)">git</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)"> clone</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)"> https://github.com/neondatabase/preview-branches-with-vercel</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="2"></span>
<span class="line" data-line="3"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-function)">cd</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)"> preview-branches-with-vercel</span></span>
<span class="line" data-line="4"></span>
<span class="line" data-line="5"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-function)">npm</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)"> install</span></span></code></pre><button class="invisible absolute right-4 border border-gray-new-80 bg-white p-1.5 text-gray-new-40 opacity-0 transition-[background-color,opacity,visibility] duration-200 group-hover/code-block:visible group-hover/code-block:opacity-100 hover:bg-gray-new-90 dark:border-gray-new-20 dark:bg-black-pure dark:text-gray-new-60 dark:hover:bg-gray-new-8 lg:visible lg:opacity-100 top-4" type="button" aria-label="Copy"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" class="h-3.5 w-3.5 text-current"><rect width="8.995" height="9.002" x="5.939" y="5.935" stroke="currentColor" rx="1"></rect><path fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" d="M2.434.935a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5 1.5v7.001a1.5 1.5 0 0 0 1.5 1.5h1.499a.5.5 0 0 0 0-1h-1.5a.5.5 0 0 1-.5-.5V2.435a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5h6.995a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v1.5a.5.5 0 1 0 1 0v-1.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5-1.5z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></button></figure>
<p>You will then need to copy the <code>.env.example</code> file to a new file called <code>.env</code>. You can do that by running the following command:</p>
<figure class="code-block group/code-block relative flex flex-col [&amp;_pre]:min-w-full" data-has-filename="false"><pre class="shiki css-variables" style="background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)" tabindex="0" data-language="bash"><code class="grid"><span class="line" data-line="1"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-function)">cp</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)"> .env.example</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-string)"> .env</span></span></code></pre><button class="invisible absolute right-4 border border-gray-new-80 bg-white p-1.5 text-gray-new-40 opacity-0 transition-[background-color,opacity,visibility] duration-200 group-hover/code-block:visible group-hover/code-block:opacity-100 hover:bg-gray-new-90 dark:border-gray-new-20 dark:bg-black-pure dark:text-gray-new-60 dark:hover:bg-gray-new-8 lg:visible lg:opacity-100 top-[min(1rem,calc(50%-.8175rem))]" type="button" aria-label="Copy"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" class="h-3.5 w-3.5 text-current"><rect width="8.995" height="9.002" x="5.939" y="5.935" stroke="currentColor" rx="1"></rect><path fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" d="M2.434.935a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5 1.5v7.001a1.5 1.5 0 0 0 1.5 1.5h1.499a.5.5 0 0 0 0-1h-1.5a.5.5 0 0 1-.5-.5V2.435a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5h6.995a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v1.5a.5.5 0 1 0 1 0v-1.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5-1.5z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></button></figure>
<p>Next, add the following environment variables which you can get from the Neon console. Add the database credentials:</p>
