onments#preview-environments\",\"children\":\"preview environment\"}],\". We will use \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://vercel.com/\",\"children\":\"Vercel\"}],\" as an example deployment provider and \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://github.com/features/actions\",\"children\":\"GitHub actions\"}],\" as the  CI/CD tool.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"staging-environments-and-why-they-are-not-ideal\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Staging environments and why they are not ideal\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#staging-environments-and-why-they-are-not-ideal\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Staging environments and why they are not ideal\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeLinecap\":\"square\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"strokeWidth\":1.4,\"d\":\"m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75\"}]}]}]]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Teams often set up a production-like environment, known as “staging”, where they test and validate new features before releasing them. The goal of this pattern is to ensure quality; however, it introduces challenges when you have several developers collaborating on the same project:\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"If the staging environment goes down, the entire team cannot preview their changes before deploying to production.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"If a developer wants to preview their changes in isolation, they will prevent other team members from deploying to the staging environment.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"You likely end up with a queue of changes that need to be reviewed, forcing you into doing a big release that includes several changes. The problem with doing a big release is that if something goes wrong unexpectedly, and you’re unsure of the cause, you must undo all of your changes.\"}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Thankfully, a new pattern is becoming increasingly popular: \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"preview environments\"}],\".\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"preview-environments-a-better-way-to-build-software\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Preview environments: A better way to build software\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#preview-environments-a-better-way-to-build-software\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Preview environments: A better way to build software\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5\",\"children\":\"$57:2:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Rather than having a shared and fixed staging environment where all developers collaborate, you automatically provision a production-like environment for every new code change a developer wants to introduce. In other words, every pull request will have its own isolated, production-like environment.\"}],\"\\n\",\"$L5f\",\"\\n\",\"$L60\",\"\\n\",\"$L61\",\"\\n\",\"$L62\",\"\\n\",\"$L63\",\"\\n\",\"$L64\",\"\\n\",\"$L65\",\"\\n\",\"$L66\",\"\\n\",\"$L67\",\"\\n\",\"$L68\",\"\\n\",\"$L69\",\"\\n\",\"$L6a\",\"\\n\",\"$L6b\",\"\\n\",\"$L6c\",\"\\n\",\"$L6d\",\"\\n\",\"$L6e\",\"\\n\",\"$L6f\",\"\\n\",\"$L70\",\"\\n\",\"$L71\",\"\\n\",\"$L72\",\"\\n\",\"$L73\",\"\\n\",\"$L74\",\"\\n\",\"$L75\",\"\\n\",\"$L76\",\"\\n\",\"$L77\",\"\\n\",\"$L78\",\"\\n\",\"$L79\",\"\\n\",\"$L7a\",\"\\n\",\"$L7b\",\"\\n\",\"$L7c\",\"\\n\",\"$L7d\",\"\\n\",\"$L7e\",\"\\n\",\"$L7f\",\"\\n\",\"$L80\",\"\\n\",\"$L81\",\"\\n\",\"$L82\",\"\\n\",\"$L83\",\"\\n\",\"$L84\",\"\\n\",\"$L85\",\"\\n\",\"$L86\",\"\\n\",\"$L87\",\"\\n\",\"$L88\",\"\\n\",\"$L89\",\"\\n\",\"$L8a\",\"\\n\",\"$L8b\",\"\\n\",\"$L8c\",\"\\n\",\"$L8d\",\"\\n\",\"$L8e\",\"\\n\",\"$L8f\",\"\\n\",\"$L90\",\"\\n\",\"$L91\",\"\\n\",\"$L92\",\"\\n\",\"$L93\",\"\\n\",\"$L94\",\"\\n\",\"$L95\",\"\\n\",\"$L96\",\"\\n\",\"$L97\",\"\\n\",\"$L98\",\"\\n\",\"$L99\",\"\\n\",\"$L9a\",\"\\n\",\"$L9b\",\"\\n\",\"$L9c\",\"\\n\",\"$L9d\",\"\\n\",\"$L9e\",\"\\n\",\"$L9f\",\"\\n\",\"$La0\",\"\\n\",\"$La1\",\"\\n\",\"$La2\",\"\\n\",\"$La3\",\"\\n\",\"$La4\",\"\\n\",\"$La5\",\"\\n\",\"$La6\",\"\\n\",\"$La7\",\"\\n\",\"$La8\",\"\\n\",\"$La9\",\"\\n\",\"$Laa\",\"\\n\",\"$Lab\",\"\\n\",\"$Lac\",\"\\n\",\"$Lad\",\"\\n\",\"$Lae\",\"\\n\",\"$Laf\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb0\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb1\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb2\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb3\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb4\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb5\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb6\"]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"b7:I[205411,[\"/_next/static/chunks/0-0o8zjuqab7b.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0-wyrs755k4-p.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0i.l9589uvx0j.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07n~9r3bo6_t_.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/05jguszscqe2t.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0bgb1-s946o7g.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/15lxb7jjl82fj.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/13twdpqxz8tr6.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0mbd~fobjqaya.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0t1wtc-7-~e~c.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07kiqkba00.os.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0ni~d5qt~j59u.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0g_miwgby_mg4.js?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7\"],\"default\"]\n:HL[\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/preview-environments-1024x576-ee4deb9b.png\",\"image\"]\n:HL[\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/301940761-1814eb55-557b-4d1c-8136-908c816dabd4-1024x576-65eb2e62.png\",\"image\"]\n:HL[\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/neons-object-hierarchy-1024x576-5d2711dd.png\",\"image\"]\n:HL[\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/image-12-1024x640-60674459.png\",\"image\"]\n:HL[\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/image-13-1024x640-160206fa.png\",\"image\"]\n:HL[\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/image-14-1024x640-2ce1bb63.png\",\"image\"]\n:HL[\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/creating-a-branch-for-every-preview-environment-1024x576-b99cb9f4.png\",\"image\"]\n:HL[\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/seeing-the-flow-in-action-1024x576-66a421c6.png\",\"image\"]\n:HL[\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/a-look-at-the-github-actions-1024x576-26f04fa7.png\",\"image\"]\n5f:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/preview-environments-1024x576-ee4deb9b.png\",\"isDark\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/preview-environments-1024x576-ee4deb9b.png\",\"alt\":\"Image\"}]}]}]\n60:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"This enables developers to build new features in parallel without affecting each other. It also makes it possible to do frequent small releases, making it easier to revert changes if something goes wrong.\"}]\n61:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Many deployment platforms are starting to support this flow out of the box by enabling you to set up an automatic Git integration. This way, you do not have to worry about maintaining and managing the necessary infrastructure for handling this flow.\"}]\n62:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"working-with-databases-in-preview-environments\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Working with databases in preview environments\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#working-with-databases-in-preview-environments\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Working with databases in preview environments\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5\",\"children\":\"$57:2:props:children"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,":1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n63:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"When teams want to set up preview environments for an app that is backed by a database, they typically pick one of the following approaches:\"}]\n64:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Setting up a shared database for all previews\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Creating a database for every pull request and seeding it with random data\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Creating a database for every pull request and seeding it with production data\"}],\"\\n\"]}]\n65:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"All of these options are not ideal and present their own drawbacks.\"}]\n66:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Creating a database for every pull request and seeding it with random data means that preview environments will not accurately represent production. So you will not be able to make changes to your production database confidently.\"}]\n67:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"The alternative would be to create a database for every pull request and import a backup of the production database. The problem with this flow is that depending on the size of your database, it can take a long time to deploy a preview environment.\"}]\n68:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"That is why teams often skip the step of creating a database for every preview and just use a shared database. The drawback is that any changes made to that shared database will impact all active previews. So, if a developer’s changes include evolving the database schema, they must notify their team members about this change and potentially prevent them from deploying. Furthermore, if the shared database goes down, no one will be able to create preview environments. This flow is somewhat similar to having a staging environment, but now the database is the bottleneck.\"}]\n69:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"The great news is that you can use Neon’s \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://neon.tech/docs/introduction/branching?utm_source=devday\u0026utm_medium=blogpost\u0026utm_campaign=blog\",\"children\":\"branching feature\"}],\" to create a production-like database for every preview. This database will contain production data and can be created in seconds.\"]}]\n6a:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"what-is-neon\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"What is Neon?\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#what-is-neon\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to What is Neon?\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5\",\"children\":\"$57:2:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n6b:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Neon is fully managed serverless Postgres. This means you don’t have to pick a size for your database upfront, and it will automatically allocate resources to meet your database’s workload.\"}]\n6c:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"To get started, go ahead and \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://neon.tech/?utm_source=devday\u0026utm_medium=blogpost\u0026utm_campaign=blog\",\"children\":\"create an account\"}],\". Next, you will want to create a new project. Choose a Postgres version, pick the region that’s closest to where you want to deploy your app. After you create the project, you will get a connection string that you can use to connect to your database.\"]}]\n6d:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/301940761-1814eb55-557b-4d1c-8136-908c816dabd4-1024x576-65eb2e62.png\",\"isDark\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/301940761-1814eb55-557b-4d1c-8136-908c816dabd4-1024x576-65eb2e62.png\",\"alt\":\"Image\"}]}]}]\n6e:[\"$\",\"blockquote\",null,{\"c"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"hildren\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Neon’s architecture separates storage and compute. This makes a Neon Postgres instance stateless, which makes it possible to automatically scale compute resources up or down based on demand.  To learn more, check out \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://neon.tech/docs/introduction/architecture-overview?utm_source=devday\u0026utm_medium=blogpost\u0026utm_campaign=blog\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noreferrer noopener\",\"children\":\"Neon’s architecture\"}],\".\"]}]}]\n6f:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"neons-object-hierarchy\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Neon’s object hierarchy\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#neons-object-hierarchy\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Neon’s object hierarchy\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3\",\"children\":\"$57:2:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n70:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"When you create a project in Neon, a default Postgres cluster is created with a default database called \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"neondb\"}],\".  Within a project’s Postgres cluster, you can have many databases. \"]}]\n71:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/neons-object-hierarchy-1024x576-5d2711dd.png\",\"isDark\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/neons-object-hierarchy-1024x576-5d2711dd.png\",\"alt\":\"Image\"}]}]}]\n72:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"This is important to know because it will help you understand how Neon’s branching feature works.\"}]\n73:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"neon-branching\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Neon branching\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#neon-branching\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Neon branching\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3\",\"children\":\"$57:2:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n74:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Neon enables you to create copies of your project’s Postgres cluster, where each copy is completely isolated from the other. We call this copying process “branching” and call each copy a “branch”.\"}]\n75:[\"$\",\"figure\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"video\",null,{\"autoPlay\":true,\"playsInline\":true,\"muted\":true,\"loop\":true,\"width\":\"1920\",\"height\":\"1080\",\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/videos/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/branching-dbe66c0d.mp4\"}]}]\n76:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"The default Postgres cluster that gets created along with a new project is represented by a branch called \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"main\"}],\".\"]}]\n77:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Neon branches are:\"}]\n78:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Isolated\"}],\": changes made to a branch don’t affect its parent\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Fast to create\"}],\": creating a branch takes ~1 second, regardless of the size of your database.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Cost-effective\"}],\": you’re only billed for unique data across all branches, and they scale to zero when not "])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"in use (you can configure this behavior for every branch).\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Ready to use\"}],\": branches will have the parent branch’s schema and all its data (you can also include data up to a certain point in time)\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n79:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"creating-a-branch-in-the-neon-console\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Creating a branch in the Neon console\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#creating-a-branch-in-the-neon-console\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Creating a branch in the Neon console\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3\",\"children\":\"$57:2:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n7a:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"To see branching in action, you will first need to create a new table and add some data to it.  Navigate to the SQL Editor and add the following SQL query.\"}]\n7c:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"This query creates a new table called \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"elements\"}],\". The table has three columns: \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"element_name\"}],\", \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"atomic_number\"}],\", and \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"symbol\"}],\". You are then inserting ten elements into that table.\"]}]\n7d:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"You can check that the data was added by going to the “Tables” page. You will find that you have a table called \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"elements\"}],\" with ten items.\"]}]\n7e:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/image-12-1024x640-60674459.png\",\"isDark\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/image-12-1024x640-60674459.png\",\"alt\":\"Image\"}]}]}]\n7f:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"To create a branch, go to the “Branches” page, and click “New Branch”. You will then be redirected to the branch creation page.\"}]\n80:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/image-13-1024x640-160206fa.png\",\"isDark\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/image-13-1024x640-160206fa.png\",\"alt\":\"Image\"}]}]}]\n81:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Here, you will first need to specify the parent branch that will be copied. Right now, you only have the main branch, but you can create a branch from other branches as well.\"}]\n82:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"You will then need to specify the data you want to include. For that, you have several options:\"}]\n83:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Current point in time\"}],\": this will include all of the available data\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Specific date and time\"}],\": this enables you to include all data up to a certain point in time. This is useful if you want to restore your branch to a previous state. You can create a branch from any previous point in time as long as it falls within your \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://neon.tech/docs/introduction/point-in-time-restore#history-retention\",\"children\":\"history-retention window\"}],\".\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Specific Log Sequence Number\"}],\": include data up to a certain LSN in the database log. This option allows for precise data recovery\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n84:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Choose the main branch as the parent, pick the “\",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Curren"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"t point in time\"}],\"” option, and click “Create new branch”. You will get a new connection string that is different than the main branch. This connection string will be associated with the newly created branch.\"]}]\n85:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/image-14-1024x640-2ce1bb63.png\",\"isDark\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/image-14-1024x640-2ce1bb63.png\",\"alt\":\"Image\"}]}]}]\n86:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"If you go to the tables page, you can select the newly created branch, and you will find that it contains all of the main branch’s data.\"}]\n87:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Now, to test that branches are isolated from one another, go back to the SQL Editor, select the newly created branch from the branch selector drop-down in the top-right of the console, and run the following query:\"}]\n89:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"This query adds ten more items to the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"elements\"}],\" table. If you go back to the tables page, you will be able to compare the difference in data between the newly created branch and the main branch.\"]}]\n8a:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"creating-a-branch-for-every-preview-environment\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Creating a branch for every Preview environment\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#creating-a-branch-for-every-preview-environment\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Creating a branch for every Preview environment\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5\",\"children\":\"$57:2:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n8b:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Neon offers an \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://api-docs.neon.tech/reference/getting-started-with-neon-api?utm_source=devday\u0026utm_medium=blogpost\u0026utm_campaign=blog\",\"children\":\"API\"}],\" that you can use to manage resources programmatically. You can use it along with a CI/CD tool to achieve the following flow:\"]}]\n8c:[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"A developer will work on changes locally against a local Postgres instance or a Neon branch. These changes could potentially include schema changes.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"They will then open a pull request which triggers a CI/CD workflow that does the following:\",\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Creates a Neon branch\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Applies database migrations if there are any\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Creates a preview deployment and uses the newly created Neon branch for the database\"}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"If everything looks good in the preview environment, the developer will merge their changes. This will trigger another CI/CD workflow that deploys the app to production. This workflow does the following:\",\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Applies the database migrations to the primary Neon branch\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Creates a production deployment\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Deletes the old Neon preview branch, which is no longer needed\"}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n8d:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/creating-a-branch-for-every-preview-environment-1024x576-b99cb9f4.png\",\"isDark\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/creating-a-branch-for-every-previ"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ew-environment-1024x576-b99cb9f4.png\",\"alt\":\"Image\"}]}]}]\n8e:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"seeing-the-flow-in-action\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Seeing the flow in action\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#seeing-the-flow-in-action\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Seeing the flow in action\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5\",\"children\":\"$57:2:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n8f:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"setting-up-the-demo-project-locally\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Setting up the demo project locally\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#setting-up-the-demo-project-locally\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Setting up the demo project locally\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3\",\"children\":\"$57:2:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n90:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"To see the flow in action, we created a demo app that displays the data coming from the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"elements\"}],\" table that we created previously. The app is built using \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://nextjs.org/\",\"children\":\"Next.js\"}],\", \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\"