xt step is using the Vercel CLI to build and deploy a preview that uses the Neon preview branch.\"}]\naa:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Finally, we comment on the pull request with the URL of the preview deployment, which we get from the deployment step, along with a link to the Neon console for the project branch.\"}]\nab:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb7\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/a-look-at-the-github-actions-1024x576-26f04fa7.png\",\"isDark\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"https://cdn.neonapi.io/public/images/pages/blog/branching-with-preview-environments/a-look-at-the-github-actions-1024x576-26f04fa7.png\",\"alt\":\"Image\"}]}]}]\nac:[\"$\",\"blockquote\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"It is a good idea to disable the automatic preview deployments that Vercel creates because they are now triggered using a GitHub action. To do that, you need to enable the “Ignored Build Step” field. Go to your Vercel project settings, select Git, and then add the following command: \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"if [ \\\"$VERCEL_ENV\\\" == \\\"production\\\" ]; then exit 1; else exit 0; fi\"}],\". This command causes Vercel to skip triggering a build if it’s a preview. You can learn more in this \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://vercel.com/guides/how-do-i-use-the-ignored-build-step-field-on-vercel\",\"children\":\"guide\"}],\".\"]}]}]\nad:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"When you open the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"deploy-production.yml\"}],\" file, you will see the following:\"]}]\naf:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"This workflow runs every time we push a commit to the main branch on GitHub by listening to the push event.  Next, the workflow runs any pending database migrations against the production database. It then deploys the app to production.\"}]\nb0:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Finally, if you open the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"cleanup-preview.yml\"}],\" file, you’ll see the following:\"]}]\nb2:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"This workflow runs when a pull request is closed, and it deletes the Neon preview branch that’s associated with the pull request using the official \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://github.com/neondatabase/delete-branch-action\",\"children\":\"delete branch action\"}],\". This act"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"ion takes the branch name or ID.\"]}]\nb3:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"conclusion\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Conclusion\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#conclusion\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Conclusion\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5\",\"children\":\"$57:2:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\nb4:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"In this tutorial, you learned how to provision a database for every preview environment by leveraging Neon’s branching feature along with GitHub Actions and Vercel.\"}]\nb5:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"You can swap out GitHub actions with another CI/CD tool or swap out Vercel with another deployment provider, as long as they support the preview environment workflow.  If there are other deployment providers or CI/CD tools you would like us to cover, feel free to reach out to us in our \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://community.neon.tech/\",\"children\":\"community forum\"}],\".\"]}]\nb6:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{